course: dictionary
lesson: 8811
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can change its job depending on how it is used. «Shearing» can be a thing, an action, or a word that describes something. Look at the words around it to find out which job it does in the sentence.
explain: «...an Australian merino that escaped shearing for years carried about 41 kilograms of fleece.» Escaped shearing means it was never cut, so shearing must mean cutting the wool off a sheep. Try your meaning in the sentence: escaped cutting-the-wool still makes sense.
explain: Shearing is also the -ing form of shear, which means cutting with big scissors called shears. In «shearing shed», the word shearing describes the shed. In science, a «shearing force» is different again: it pushes parts of something in opposite directions. The context always gives the clue.
fact: Shearing means cutting the wool off a sheep, usually once a year.
fact: «Shear» means to cut with big scissors called shears, or with clippers; «shearing» is its -ing form.
fact: A «shearing shed» is a building where sheep are shorn, and «shearing season» is the time of year when this happens.
fact: In science, a «shearing force» pushes parts of something in opposite directions, so it slides or breaks.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, shearers compete in shearing contests to see who can shear a sheep fastest.
exercise: In «an Australian merino that escaped shearing for years carried about 41 kilograms of fleece», what does shearing mean? | Sliding down a hill | *Cutting the wool off a sheep | Running fast across a field | Sleeping in the sun
exercise: In «shearing shed», what job does shearing do? | It tells you how many sheep there are | *It describes the shed | It is the name of a farm | It means the shed is huge
exercise: In «shearing force», what happens to the parts of something? | They are cut with big scissors | They grow longer and thinner | They are painted in bright colours | *They are pushed in opposite directions so they slide or break
test: Ella reads «shearing season» and guesses it is a season for swimming. What is shearing season most likely to be? | *The time of year when sheep are cut | The time for swimming in the sea | A season when it snows | The long summer holiday
test: Shearing means cutting the wool off a sheep. What does shearing mean in «shearing contests»? | Contests to paint the best farm | Contests to see who can sing the loudest | *Competitions to see who can shear sheep fastest | Races for sheep across a field
exam: In «a shearing force», what does shearing tell you about the forces? | They always happen in spring | They are soft and fluffy like wool | They are pushes that make things bigger | *They push parts in opposite directions so they slide or break
